  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 808242,
  "published": "2026-11-27T17:53:41.8Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.14.0: what a module's parent gives a child is a public method (MI-62). New MyIdentityPermissionOptions.GetInheritedPermissions(string childModuleCode, MyIdentityPermission parentPermission): what one row of a module's parent gives that child at the permission decision point (the value with its implications, cut to the child's SupportedPermissions with theirs; None wherever GetParentModule is null and for a None row), computed by the same internal function the decision point now uses, so a role matrix no longer copies the rule. Nothing the decision point answers changes. GETTING_STARTED §7 states the rule and the recipe for taking one permission from one child of a role that holds the parent: convert the parent's row into rows of its children in one unit of work, children first and the parent last, and announce its four consequences. No migration; nothing added to an interface. Upgrading from 5.13.0: MyIdentity/UPGRADE.md §58.",
